@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `usca-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `usca-holidays`

-- The worked cases of the brief, run through the time module with calendars built by the holidays module.  Expected values were written down
-- before the first run of the module (see NOTES.md, answer table), from the statute text and an independent script.
-- Calendars: G is Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701 for the state with nothing supplied (Sundays and the days fixed by the calendar, no Saturdays).
-- C is Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a) taking in the Sundays of § 10, with nothing supplied (Saturdays and Sundays).
-- C+ is C with the Gov. Code days supplied as the section 135 days (here only Monday 2 September 2030, the one such day these cases meet).

GIVETH A `Days supplied by the caller`
`section 135 days of the cases` MEANS
    `Days supplied by the caller` WITH
        `Lunar New Year days` IS EMPTY
        `Diwali days` IS EMPTY
        `days appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving or holiday` IS EMPTY
        `Thursdays appointed as Thanksgiving Day` IS EMPTY
        `Good Friday days` IS EMPTY
        `days on which March 31 is observed instead` IS EMPTY
        `March 31 itself stays a holiday in a year in which it is observed on another day` IS TRUE
        `judicial holidays specified in Code Civ. Proc. section 135` IS (LIST YMD 2030 9 2)
        `days a public office is closed for the whole day` IS EMPTY
        `bank closings under the Bank Extraordinary Situation Closing Act` IS EMPTY

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`calendar G` d MEANS `a holiday under Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701 for the state` `no day is supplied` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`calendar C` d MEANS `a holiday for the extension of Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), taking in the Sundays of § 10` `no day is supplied` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`calendar C plus` d MEANS `a holiday for the extension of Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), taking in the Sundays of § 10` `section 135 days of the cases` d


§ `Three years from 2025-07-16`

-- three years from 2025-07-16: the last day before the rest-day rule is 2028-07-16 (Sunday).
#ASSERT `before the rest-day rule, the last day of a period of` 3 years `counted from` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS (YMD 2028 7 16)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 years `counted from` (YMD 2025 7 16) `under the calendar` `calendar G` EQUALS (YMD 2028 7 17)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 years `counted from` (YMD 2025 7 16) `with a holiday last day excluded once under the calendar` `calendar G` EQUALS (YMD 2028 7 17)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 years `counted from` (YMD 2025 7 16) `under the calendar` `calendar C` EQUALS (YMD 2028 7 17)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 years `counted from` (YMD 2025 7 16) `with a holiday last day excluded once under the calendar` `calendar C` EQUALS (YMD 2028 7 17)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 years `counted from` (YMD 2025 7 16) `under the calendar` `calendar C plus` EQUALS (YMD 2028 7 17)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 years `counted from` (YMD 2025 7 16) `with a holiday last day excluded once under the calendar` `calendar C plus` EQUALS (YMD 2028 7 17)

